### 4. RPC Patterns Summary

Nebula uses a custom RPC abstraction called `RemoteProcess<T>` (decorated with `[NebulaRPCHolder]`) rather than vanilla `RpcInvoke`/`HandleRpc`. Key patterns:

**Pattern 1: Simple RemoteProcess (no payload)**
```csharp
public static readonly RemoteProcess RpcBreakEmergencyButton = new("BreakEmergencyButton",
    (_) => AmongUsLLImpl.ShipStatusInstance.BreakEmergencyButton());
```

**Pattern 2: RemoteProcess with tuple payload + simple handler**
```csharp
public static readonly RemoteProcess<(byte reporter, byte reported)> RpcNoticeStartMeeting = new("ModStartMeeting",
    (message, _) => { ... });
```

**Pattern 3: RemoteProcess with custom serialization/deserialization**
```csharp
public static readonly RemoteProcess<(List<VoterState> firstStates, List<(byte, byte)> mapList, byte exiled, byte[] exiledAll, bool tie, bool isObvious)> RpcModCompleteVoting = new("CompleteVoting",
    (writer, message) => { /* serialize */ },
    (reader) => { /* deserialize */ return result; },
    (message, _) => { /* handle */ });
```

**Pattern 4: RPC section grouping**
```csharp
using (RPCRouter.CreateSection("ExilePlayer")) { ... }  // from ExilePatch.cs
```

**Pattern 5: Synchronizer sync pattern**
```csharp
NebulaAPI.CurrentGame?.GetModule<Synchronizer>()?.SendSync(SynchronizeTag.PostMeeting);
yield return NebulaAPI.CurrentGame?.GetModule<Synchronizer>()?.CoSyncAndReset(Modules.SynchronizeTag.PostMeeting, true, true, false);
```

**Pattern 6: Vanilla RPC blocking**
```csharp
// Blocks vanilla VotingComplete (callId 23)
[HarmonyPatch(typeof(MeetingHud), nameof(MeetingHud.HandleRpc))]
class CancelVotingCompleteByRPCPatch
{
    public static bool Prefix(MeetingHud __instance, [HarmonyArgument(0)] byte callId)
    {
        if (callId == 23) return false;
        return true;
    }
}
```

**Pattern 7: Custom ModCastVote**
```csharp
// Instead of vanilla RpcCastVote, uses custom ModCastVote with vote weight
__instance.ModCastVote(AmongUsLLImpl.LocalPlayer.PlayerId, suspectStateIdx, vote);
```

